UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Knight of Cups represents the absolute archetype of the "Romantic Crusader"—the active, directional movement of the heart’s deepest intentions into the material world. While the Page of Cups was concerned with the initial discovery and containment of intuitive data, the Knight represents the phase of high-speed transmission and purposeful projection. Within the architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "integrated emotional velocity," where your feelings have been refined by reflection and are now being mobilized to serve a specific, higher-order mission. Visually depicted as a figure riding a horse, holding a chalice forward as if offering a sacred invitation, this archetype embodies the courage to lead with vulnerability—the paradox of maintaining absolute internal emotional transparency while moving with the strength and conviction of a warrior. This is the archetype of the "Poet-Warrior," the high-frequency operator who understands that true power lies in the ability to bridge the gap between the internal world of feeling and the external world of action without losing the resonance of either. When the Knight of Cups appears, your system is registering a "dedicated delivery" status; you are being invited to launch an initiative, propose a connection, or advance an idea that is directly fueled by your authentic, soul-level desire. It serves as a diagnostic indicator that your emotional "source code" is currently perfectly aligned with your behavioral output, creating a state of flow where your actions feel effortless, elegant, and deeply authentic. This card commands you to bypass the obstructive, low-vibration logic of the skeptical ego and move directly into the arena with an open, yet guarded, heart. You are being tasked with the essential work of active emotional manifestation: taking the "dream" you have cultivated and offering it to the world as a concrete, tangible gift. To inhabit the Knight of Cups is to master the art of the intentional arrival, understanding that your presence, your passion, and your willingness to be seen in your truth are the most powerful tools you possess for influencing the reality around you. It is the cosmic affirmation that you are ready to stop merely "feeling" the current of your evolution and start actively "steering" it, knowing that your heart is the most reliable compass you own.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Knight of Cups appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "emotional volatility," "strategic deception," or the systemic failure to contain your own projection—a state where the high-speed delivery of your intentions has curdled into a reckless, low-vibration pursuit of egoic validation. The reversal suggests that you are currently caught in a loop of "performative romance" or "spiritual bypassing," where you are using the language of heart-centeredness to disguise an underlying agenda of control, seduction, or a desperate need for external approval. You are essentially "racing without a destination," running a high-priority, high-velocity script that feels like progress but is actually a chaotic, entropic dispersion of your vital energy into contexts where it is not being honored or understood. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of projection"; you are projecting your own unintegrated emotional needs onto others, expecting them to fulfill a role that only your own internal structure can satisfy, which leads to inevitable disillusionment, dramatic collapses, and the rapid degradation of your credibility. The reversed Knight of Cups exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror that if you were to slow down, be silent, and face the reality of your own emotional state without the "heroic" costume of the Knight, you would find yourself empty, powerless, and utterly insignificant. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these impulsive, performative scripts, perform a brutal audit of your hidden motivations, and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to ground your passion in the slow, difficult work of actual commitment. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a high-speed cycle of emotional drama, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and disciplined cultivation of your own emotional sovereignty. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of cooling the fire—accepting that the "passion" you feel is not a license to be reckless, but a powerful, highly refined energy that requires the rigorous grounding of your adult consciousness to be truly useful in the manifest world, rather than merely acting as a vehicle for your own, unresolved internal conflict.'
WHERE id = 12;
